<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs-Monday actual 109,000 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs-Monday actual 109,000 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Actual interior Iowa and southern Minnesota hog marketings Monday were 109,000 head, compared with the estimate of 110,000, according to USDA.</p>
<p>Opening trade was not well established.  Early sales of Barrows and Gilts Tuesday were steady to $0.50 per cwt lower than the midsession Monday.</p>
<p>				  Country		   Plants</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>220-260 lbs	    52.00 -52.50	   53.00 -53.50</p>
<p>few			51.50  53.00	   52.50  54.00</p>
<p>Sows:  steady.</p>
<p>US 1-3  300-450 lbs. 42.00 -43.00	   42.50 -44.00</p>
<p>450-500 lbs.	   44.00 -47.00	   45.00 -47.00</p>
<p>500 lbs. up	    48.00 -50.00	   49.00 -51.00</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
